{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>But if any man hates his fellow.</b> Through his hatred he arrives at <b>and lies in wait for him</b>. From here the Sages said: if a person transgresses a minor commandment, he ends up transgressing a major one — for having transgressed ״לֹא תִשְׂנָא״ (Leviticus 19), he ends up coming to bloodshed. Therefore it is written ״וְכִי יִהְיֶה אִישׁ שֹׂנֵא לְרֵעֵהוּ״ and so forth — when it should have written ״וְכִי יָקוּם אִישׁ וְאָרַב לְרֵעֵהוּ וְהִכָּהוּ נָפֶשׁ״ (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:40.988387173Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}